---Execute a shell command.
---
---Any shell command arguments should be provided as separate argument strings to this function. If the exit code of the process is not zero, this function throws error. By default, the function returns `nil`, but it can be configured to capture the output of the shell command as string and return it — set `out` option to `"capture"` to do it.
---By default, after this shell command is executed, the editor will reload resources from disk.
---
---**Examples:**
---
---Make a directory with spaces in it:
---```
---editor.execute("mkdir", "new dir")
---```
---Read the git status:
---```
---local status = editor.execute("git", "status", "--porcelain", {
---  reload_resources = false,
---  out = "capture"
---})
---```
---@overload fun(command:string, ...:string, options?:editor.execute.options):nil|string
---@param command string Shell command name to execute
---@param ... string Optional shell command arguments
---@return nil|string result If `out` option is set to `"capture"`, returns the output as string with trimmed trailing newlines. Otherwise, returns `nil`.
---
---[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/editor-lua#editor.execute:command-...-options)
function editor.execute(command, ...) end

